Subject: freedreno/a5xx: implement get_compute_state_info

Rusticl checks at context creation that the Gallium driver provides a
get_compute_state_info callback. The a6xx Freedreno driver does (see
fd6_compute.cc); the a5xx Freedreno driver did not, so Rusticl
panicked at clCreateContext with:

  Missing context feature get_compute_state_info
  thread '<unnamed>' panicked at
    'Context missing features. This should never happen!',
    src/gallium/frontends/rusticl/mesa/pipe/context.rs:46

Add a minimal a5xx version that reports device-wide max threads,
SIMD size (= threadsize_base, the GPU's wavefront size) and zero
private memory. This is conservative compared to a6xx (which clamps
max_threads per-variant by register footprint and reports the
shader's actual pvtmem usage), but it's enough to unblock Rusticl
initialisation and lets OpenCL kernels dispatch on Adreno 5xx
(Adreno 506 on the FP3+).

Tested on Adreno 506 / SDM632 / Fairphone 3+. clinfo now enumerates
the Freedreno OpenCL platform; previously it aborted on panic
before reaching that point.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_compute.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_compute.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  */

 #include "pipe/p_state.h"
+#include "freedreno_dev_info.h"

 #include "freedreno_resource.h"

@@ -167,6 +168,19 @@ fd5_launch_grid(struct fd_context *ctx,
    }
 }

+static void
+fd5_get_compute_state_info(struct pipe_context *pctx, void *cso,
+                           struct pipe_compute_state_object_info *cinfo)
+{
+   const struct fd_dev_info *info = fd_context(pctx)->screen->info;
+   uint32_t threadsize_base = info->threadsize_base;
+
+   cinfo->max_threads = threadsize_base * info->max_waves;
+   cinfo->simd_sizes = threadsize_base;
+   cinfo->preferred_simd_size = threadsize_base;
+   cinfo->private_memory = 0;
+}
+
 void
 fd5_compute_init(struct pipe_context *pctx) disable_thread_safety_analysis
 {
@@ -174,4 +188,5 @@ fd5_compute_init(struct pipe_context *pctx) disable_thread_safety_analysis
    ctx->launch_grid = fd5_launch_grid;
    pctx->create_compute_state = ir3_shader_compute_state_create;
    pctx->delete_compute_state = ir3_shader_state_delete;
+   pctx->get_compute_state_info = fd5_get_compute_state_info;
 }
